1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,640
Ménière's disease, diagnosed in about 615,000 U.S.

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:13,680
adults with up to 100,000 new cases every year — if your vertigo comes bundled with ringing ears, hearing changes, or a plugged-up feeling, it's not just ordinary dizziness.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,640
Ménière's happens when fluid builds up in the inner ear, a condition called endolymphatic hydrops.

4
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:27,920
Unlike BPPV or vestibular neuritis, attacks bring vertigo, tinnitus, fluctuating hearing loss, and aural fullness together, and can last anywhere from twenty minutes to several hours.

5
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:33,360
Three everyday habits make attacks worse: sodium, caffeine and alcohol, and stress or poor sleep.

6
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:34,640
First, sodium.

7
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:40,480
Extra salt makes your body retain fluid, which raises pressure in the already fluid-overloaded inner ear.

8
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:47,840
Keep sodium under 1,500 to 2,000 milligrams a day, and swap canned and processed foods for fresh ingredients you season yourself.

9
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:49,920
Second, caffeine and alcohol.

10
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:58,880
Caffeine constricts blood vessels and reduces blood flow to the inner ear, while alcohol diffuses directly into the inner ear fluid and disrupts its balance — both can trigger an episode.

11
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,600
Swap coffee for decaf or herbal tea, and reach for sparkling water instead of a second drink.

12
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:06,400
Third, stress and inconsistent sleep.

13
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:12,080
Both disrupt the nervous system signals that regulate blood flow and fluid balance in the inner ear.

14
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:16,960
Keep a consistent sleep schedule, and swap your phone before bed for a few minutes of light stretching.

15
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:24,080
If vertigo keeps showing up with ringing ears or hearing changes, don't just wait it out — see an ENT for a proper diagnosis.

16
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:29,520
Cutting back on sodium, caffeine, and alcohol, plus steady sleep, meaningfully cuts down how often attacks happen.
